=== Module 23 - Left Recursion Elimination ===

direct:   A -> A a | b        ==>   A -> b A'    A' -> a A' | epsilon
indirect: Paull's algorithm -- fix an order, substitute lower nonterminals
          into higher ones, then remove direct left recursion.

########## fixtures/expr.grammar

BEFORE:
  E -> E + T | T
  T -> T * F | F
  F -> ( E ) | id | num
  left-recursive? true

AFTER (Paull):
  E -> T E'
  E' -> + T E' | epsilon
  T -> F T'
  T' -> * F T' | epsilon
  F -> ( E ) | id | num
  left-recursive? false
  start symbol: E

language check (all strings up to length 6):
  before: 70 strings
  after : 70 strings
  identical? true
  sample: "( ( id ) )"  "( ( num ) )"  "( id )"  "( id ) * id"  "( id ) * num"  "( id ) + id"  "( id ) + num"  "( id * id )"  

########## fixtures/indirect.grammar

BEFORE:
  S -> A a | b
  A -> A c | S d | e
  left-recursive? true

AFTER (Paull):
  S -> A a | b
  A -> b d A' | e A'
  A' -> c A' | a d A' | epsilon
  left-recursive? false
  start symbol: S

language check (all strings up to length 6):
  before: 20 strings
  after : 20 strings
  identical? true
  sample: "b"  "b d a"  "b d a d a"  "b d a d c a"  "b d c a"  "b d c a d a"  "b d c c a"  "b d c c c a"  

